Overlay patch 0019 - iOS supersampling (SSAA) and the sub-native fix.

CLASS: (a) program-baseline parity. Cross-port adoption of Lighthouse's overlay
0036 (itself Ghostship's 0032, device-confirmed), re-authored against this
port's LUS fork (`JeodC/libultraship`, branch `lus-converge`).

THE RULE (docs/parity-checklist.md, "The two rules, exactly")
------------------------------------------------------------
In `Interpreter::StartFrame`, after the `mCurDimensions.height == 0` guard and
BEFORE the framebuffer-resize block, scale `mCurDimensions` ONLY, by

    f = (nativeDrawablePxLongEdge / mCurDimensions.width) * ssaa

clamped to `mRapi->GetMaxTextureSize()`. `mNativeDimensions` and
`mGameWindowViewport` are untouched: their uses are equality-guarded and
deactivate to the safe full-framebuffer path.

WHY THE FACTOR IS NATIVE-PX-RELATIVE
------------------------------------
`Fast3dGui::CalculateGameViewport` sets `mCurDimensions` from the "Main Game"
ImGui window's content region, and `ImGui::Image` then scales the offscreen
game framebuffer up to the native-pixel fb0. Whether that content region
arrives in points (the sibling ports' finding: iPhone rendered 1824x840 into a
2736x1260 drawable, 67 %) or already in drawable pixels (which is what this
fork's `io.DisplaySize` implies on iOS - the design notes D16), the ratio form lands
the render on exactly `nativePx * ssaa`. It is therefore self-correcting: with
ssaa = 1.0 the render is native, never sub-native and never above it.

`internal_mul` (the Internal Resolution slider) cancels out of the same
expression, which is why overlay 0020 pins and greys that widget rather than
leaving a slider that cannot move a pixel.

THE SHELL'S TWO HOOKS
---------------------
    extern "C" float    PBIos_SsaaFactor(void);        // gSohIos.Supersample
    extern "C" uint32_t PBIos_DrawablePixelWidth(void); // CAMetalLayer px, long edge

Both live in `app/ios/PaperBoatIosShell.m` (the same linkage pattern as
`PBIos_IsBackgrounded` in overlay 0008 and `PBIos_GetSafeAreaInsets` in 0013).
`PBIos_SsaaFactor` reads the CVar and falls back to a Metal-GPU-family device
tier (Apple8 -> 2.0, Apple7 -> 1.5, else 1.0) when it is unset; the shell, not
this file, owns those defaults. A 0 from either hook means "not ready yet" and
this block does nothing at all, which is byte-identical to upstream.

CVAR BLOCK: `gSohIos.*`, deliberately - the family-wide harbour-shell block,
kept verbatim so the eventual extraction does not have to rename anything.
Recorded in the shell divergence notes.

WHAT IT EXPORTS BACK
--------------------
`gPBIosSsaaW` / `gPBIosSsaaH`, the effective dimensions, for the bridge's
`ssaa` verb. They are also SPDLOG'd once per change, which is the artifact the
spec's rule 6 asks for on a claim like "2.0x doubles the render".

`__IOS__`-only, so the macOS oracle stays pristine.

WHERE THE HUNK SITS
-------------------
One hunk, in and immediately above `Interpreter::StartFrame` (~:7020). No other
patch in the series touches `external/libultraship/src/fast/interpreter.cpp`.

Match-count asserted against the pristine vendor state.

